@doc email_chain
@meta title: Email chain in which an employee writes about their own leave and grievance
@meta subject: RE: My leave and the grievance
@meta traps: an employee writing from their work address about their own leave, health or grievance is a third party in that message, and so are their name, title and work address (K2 trap: an official's own grievance or medical leave is not about the position); the HR adviser answering is acting in their role
@cast employee=official adviser=official manager=official requester=requester
@block email_header
From: {adviser.full_name} <{adviser.work_email}>
Sent: Tuesday, 9 June, 3:20 PM
To: {employee.full_name!R1} <{employee.work_email!R1}>
Subject: RE: My leave and the grievance

@block body
Thank you for sending the medical note. Your leave is approved from 15 June and I have
told your manager only that you will be away, not why. The grievance you filed about the
scheduling decision is with the labour relations unit and you will hear from them directly.

A client file in your queue, {requester.full_name}'s, will be reassigned while you are away.

@block signature
{adviser.full_name}
{adviser.title}
{adviser.organisation}
{adviser.work_phone}

@block email_header
From: {employee.full_name!R1} <{employee.work_email!R1}>
Sent: Monday, 8 June, 8:47 AM
To: {adviser.full_name} <{adviser.work_email}>
Cc: {manager.full_name} <{manager.work_email}>
Subject: My leave and the grievance

@block body
I am attaching the note from my doctor. I would like to start leave on 15 June and I do
not want the reason shared with the team. I also want to confirm that my grievance about
the change to my schedule has been received.

You can reach me at home on {employee.personal_phone!R1} while I am off.

@block signature
{employee.full_name!R1}
{employee.title!R1}
{employee.work_phone!R1}
